IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itra-rates`

-- Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Cth) -- worked cases from the seat of the taxpayer: s 3, s 3A, ss 16-20(1), Schedule 7 Parts I-III, ss 23(2), 23(6),
-- 23AA, 23AB.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case or an ATO publication. Fixtures are generated by scratchpad gen_income-tax-rates-act-1986_baseline.py;
-- expected results were written by hand from the deposited text.
--
-- The lives (workbench scenarios/au/wa): chloe c045 (2024-10-20), the 2023-24 return, taxable income $27,500, scenario
-- expects nil tax after the low income tax offset; chloe c048 (2025-10-25), the 2024-25 return, taxable income $71,500,
-- scenario records "tax_before_offsets": 12842; daniel d04a (2033-11-30), Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd's first company
-- return, "What rate; is a loss carried forward?". The scenario puts Jarrah under $3 million turnover until 2036; its income
-- figures and the loss year here are ASSUMED. The s 20(1) and Schedule 7 clause 2 formulas are those transcribed by hand from
-- the authorised rendering in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.formulas.md.
--
-- Agreement with ../../../income-tax-assessment-act-1997/encodings/baseline-2026-10 (itaa-cases-income.l4), which restates
-- these rates: $18,200 threshold; c045 2023-24 $1,767 (REQ-0056, from Compilation No. 62); c048 $12,238; k043 (Jake, 2028-29, $31,000) $1,792; a company
-- with no passive income and $3 million turnover 25%; one 90% passive 30%. The same figures are asserted below.

