§ `Schedule 7 -- remainders, working holiday makers, non-residents, part-year residents`

-- Super remainder: OTI 71,500 -> 12,238 + 20,000 x 45% = 21,238. ETP remainder: 12,238 + 4,500 = 16,738.
-- WHM all on visa: 30,000 x 15% = 4,500. WHM 20,000 of 60,000: 3,000 + (8,788 - 288) = 11,500.
-- Non-residents: 9,000; 40,500 + 5,550 = 46,050; 40,500 + 20,350 + 4,500 = 65,350. Non-resident WHM: 6,750 + 1,500 = 8,250.
-- Pensioner abroad: resident taxpayer, 11,800 x 16% = 1,888. Arrival in October (9 months, s 18(1)(b)): threshold 17,016,
-- (30,000 - 17,016) x 16% = 2,077.44; an eligible pensioner has no part-year residency period (s 18(2)(a)): 1,888.
-- Clause 2, author: special income component 100,000, reduced taxable income 50,000. A = 4,288 + 5,000 x 30% = 5,788.
-- Tax on 50,000 + 20,000 = 70,000 is 11,788; B = 5 x (11,788 - 5,788) = 30,000. A + B = 35,788 (36,838 without clause 2).
-- Division 392 averaging (clause 3) is not encoded. Non-resident, Part II clause 2: A = 30,000 x 30% = 9,000; B = 5 x
-- (36,000 - 30,000) x 30% = 9,000; 18,000, the same as the flat 30% band without clause 2.
